# FastGram Architecture Rules

## Layers
- Interface: `app/bot/`, `app/api/` (receive input, call services)
- Application: `app/modules/*/service.py` (business logic)
- Domain: `app/modules/*/models.py` (data models)
- Infrastructure: `app/modules/*/repository.py` (DB access)
- Core: `app/core/` (config, DB, logging)

## Session Rules
- Use `session_scope` from `app/core/db.py` when DB access is needed.
- Controllers (handlers/routes) never open DB sessions.
- Services own session lifecycle.
- Repositories receive a session from callers; repositories never create sessions.

## Module Layout
- Each module must include:
  - `models.py`
  - `repository.py`
  - `service.py`
  - `schemas.py`
- Modules must remain pure and must not import framework transport objects.
- Do not import in `app/modules/*`:
  - `aiogram`
  - `fastapi.Request`
  - Telegram update/message objects

## Handler and Route Rules
- Handlers/routes stay thin: parse input, call service, return/send output.
- Do not query DB directly in handlers/routes.
- Do not place business logic in handlers/routes.

## Where to Add Features
- Order logic: `app/modules/orders/service.py`
- Order DB queries: `app/modules/orders/repository.py`
- New API endpoint: `app/api/routes/`
- New bot command: `app/bot/handlers/`
- External API calls: `app/integrations/`

## DO / DON'T
- DO: handlers call services.
- DO: services call repositories.
- DO: use `session_scope` in service layer when DB is needed.
- DO: keep modules pure.
- DON'T: put DB queries in handlers.
- DON'T: put business logic in routes.
- DON'T: import `aiogram` inside modules.
